<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#slave-raiding">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Slave raiding</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Slave raiding is the capture of people by force to be enslaved and sold or used for labour. It was an important economic activity of many states of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sahel">Sahel</a>, which raided neighbouring peoples to supply trans-Saharan and other markets. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wadai-empire">Wadai Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darfur-sultanate">Darfur Sultanate</a> profiles describe slave raiding as a major source of wealth and a cause of regional conflict.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/slave-raiding.jpg" alt="Slave raiding" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Slave_Raid,_Africa,_ca.1800-ca.1865_(imp-cswc-GB-237-CSWC47-LS16-029).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
